{"id": "EUVD-2026-93173", "enisaUuid": "1fb0d2bc-0fd4-305b-8728-0ae53343f99d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: take commit root semaphore when iterating in mark_block_group_to_copy()\n\nmark_block_group_to_copy() iterates over the commit root with\nskip_locking=true. A concurrent transaction commit can swap and free\nthe commit root during iteration, causing use-after-free when\naccessing extent buffers.\n\nFix it by using path->need_commit_sem to protect the commit root search.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93a025166495c63ba5b8ac721c7040d5312e8335", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e2007b263ea250251ec3021a0a197da990ee1a8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/709f6a5e986535005110c6c69b322f63631cb200", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c32490c6d3f3a9f2d177d57c7eb8bbc347561d08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0594e3423f4ba3137c734371169491f9a98e9af4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-crm6-8p5c-4rv5", "CVE-2026-98245"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00a6ef72-0a48-3e3f-9d80-4909bd8acf91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78ce9fc269af6e69c1399ab910ba6bc81c934f67 <8e2007b263ea250251ec3021a0a197da990ee1a8"}, {"id": "254fea18-3dd5-305a-a52f-583fb366ded4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "54c971e9-eccf-3c86-9790-06dcc7bba8ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78ce9fc269af6e69c1399ab910ba6bc81c934f67 <709f6a5e986535005110c6c69b322f63631cb200"}, {"id": "55067fa3-e6fd-3a65-8941-73bc7ebd21fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "57ac774d-0873-3ade-9fcf-66136514490e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "78ce9fc269af6e69